# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metaldraw).
#
# The first triangle through Metal on this GPU, with one of Apple's own fragment shaders and
# nothing else in the boot, so that "did it draw" cannot be answered by a log whose middle was
# dropped.
#
# clearFragment20 writes render target 2 and is one of the 255 fragment shaders air_run has
# drawn and compared pixel by pixel on softpipe, so there is a reference: with its 48-byte
# constant buffer filled (i * 7 + 13) & 0xff, softpipe gives
#
#     2458616957 2930221209 3401825461 3873429713
#
# The pipeline is asked for with no vertex function, which is the compiler library's cue to
# supply the pass-through stage air_run itself draws over. This exercises the whole render
# path: vertex and tiler jobs, the fragment job, the render target and the readback.
#
# say_run puts every line in the kernel log (a job's stdout is kept nowhere); if the test dies,
# the line after it still turns the properties off.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props show
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props on
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props off
